# Lane search: the per-day record files only. They are the search log, 18 KB a record and
# over a gigabyte a day, and single files already past GitHub's 100 MB limit. A lanesearch
# record is a pure function of code, candidate and parameters, so a dropped one regenerates
# exactly. ledger.jsonl and elites.json stay tracked: the ledger is the identity and summary
# of every candidate at 392 bytes each, and elites.json is a published traceability source
# (DECISIONS.md D40), so a number on a page has to trace to a committed artifact. The git
# boundary is the same one D40 drew for the traceability list.
adaptive_archive/20*.jsonl
implicit_archive/20*.jsonl
